<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Thanjavur Maratha Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1674 CE – 1855 CE · capital Thanjavur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Maratha kingdom in the Tamil Kaveri delta, founded by Shivaji's half-brother and celebrated for the Saraswati Mahal library and Tanjore painting.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1674 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ekoji-i">Venkoji</a> (Ekoji I), half-brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> and a general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a> sultanate, seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> from its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayak</a> rulers and founded a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhonsles">Bhonsle</a> dynasty there. It thus became a Marathi-speaking court ruling a Tamil land.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Rajas ruled the rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> lands of the Kaveri delta, surviving pressure from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carnatic-sultanate">Carnatic Nawabs</a> and Mysore. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serfoji-ii">Serfoji II</a>, whose administration was largely ceded to the British in 1799, expanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saraswati-mahal-library">Saraswati Mahal</a> library and patronised Carnatic music, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Tanjore</a> painting and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji-of-thanjavur">Shivaji II</a> died in 1855 without a male heir, the British annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> under the doctrine of lapse. The palace, library and the painting style it fostered survive in Thanjavur.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/thanjavur-maratha-kingdom.jpg" alt="Thanjavur Maratha Kingdom" width="320" height="245"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Thanjavur_Maratha_kingdom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1674 CE – 1855 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thanjavur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Venkoji, Serfoji II, Shivaji II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Marathi, Tamil</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tanjore, Kingdom of Thanjavur</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1764&amp;focus=thanjavur-maratha-kingdom" aria-label="Thanjavur Maratha Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6860 1775 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Thanjavur Maratha Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7180 2031L7180 2031M7180 2031L7364 1601"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7180 2031h0M7364 1601h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7180 2031h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7180 2031h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Thanjavur. <a href="/atlas?year=1764&amp;focus=thanjavur-maratha-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
